Version Beta-2 0.12.1
=====
- NOTE: slacker-cli (v0.12.1) has no changes, this version has fixes for slacker-gui only(vBeta_2).
- Update: slacker-gui
    - font sizes follow the desktop. The stylesheet pinned a dozen sizes in
      absolute points, so those parts of the window ignored the font size set in
      the desktop while the rest followed it; they are ratios now, and
      everything scales together. Reported by @danix (issue #9).
    - zoom: Ctrl with the wheel, or Ctrl with +, - and 0, scales the whole
      window between 70% and 250% of the desktop's font size. The choice is
      remembered in ~/.config/slacker-gui/zoom.
    - blocks of slacker's own output are no longer clipped when the font is
      large. They were drawn in a TextView, which is scrollable and therefore
      has a minimum height of zero, so inside a preferences group it collapsed;
      a label measures the text it holds.
- Fix: slacker-gui
    - the "nothing has been printed" notice no longer appears during kernel
      upgrades, when dracut is simply quiet while it builds the initrd. It now
      waits much longer unless the last line really reads like a question, and
      when it does appear it says so calmly instead of looking like an error.
