Version Beta 0.12.1
=====
- Update: man page and wiki pages
- Update: cmd: slacker show-changelog for repos: {alienbob,restricted,patches,extras,testing}
- Update: cmd:slacker find-mirror suggest only mirros in sync
- Update: rc.local_shutdown added to protected files too.
- Update: prepare slacker code for aarch64 support.
- Fix: cmd:slacker status
    - the Pkgtools row no longer reports installpkg/upgradepkg/removepkg as
      MISSING when `status` runs as a plain user. Slackware's /etc/profile puts
      /sbin on root's PATH only, so a user (or slacker-gui, which runs `status`
      unprivileged) saw a false error. The check now looks on $PATH and in
      /sbin. Nothing changed in how the pkgtools are executed: they still run
      as root, where /sbin is on the PATH.
- Update: cmd:slacker revert-pkg
    - the cumulative archive is now read BEFORE you are asked to choose a
      version, so an archive that cannot serve the rollback is reported up
      front instead of after the selection.
    - three situations that used to end in the same confusing message are now
      told apart: an archive that answers with a package list that has no
      packages yet, an address that does not return a package list at all
      (a typo in CUMULATIVE_URL, an error page), and an archive that cannot be
      reached. A package that is not in the list at all is also reported
      before the prompt.
    - when the package is listed but that particular build is no longer in the
      tree, slacker prints the exact URL where the release archive keeps it and
      the CUMULATIVE_URL to set if you want it. It never switches archive by
      itself: which repository to trust stays the admin's decision.
    - why this matters: from 16.0 on, slackware.uk moves the whole cumulative
      -current tree into the archive of the release when that release is made,
      and copies the fresh release package set back in its place. Signatures
      travel with the packages, so verification is unaffected, but for a while
      after each release the -current archive holds one version per package and
      has nothing older to offer. That is now a clear message, not an error.
- Fix: shared code on non-x86 architectures (no change on x86)
    - `status` no longer compares your mirror against the x86 tree on the
      upstream reference mirror when the system is not x86. That reference
      carries no Slackware ARM trees, so the freshness verdict was meaningless
      there; it is now reported as not checked.
    - `find-mirror` stops with an explanation instead of probing the official
      mirror list, which lists x86 trees only, and proposing lines for the
      wrong architecture.
    - the kernel reminder now also recognises Slackware ARM's `kernel_armv8`,
      and the LILO/ELILO/GRUB line is printed only for an x86 kernel package.
    - the default CUMULATIVE_URL on aarch64 points at the aarch64 cumulative
      tree instead of the 32-bit x86 one.
