Version Beta 0.11.0
=====
Add: resolve-stock - pull an official package's STOCK deps on minimal/container systems (only for x86_64)
https://github.com/rizitis/slackware64-current-ci/pkgs/container/slackware64-current-ci

WHAT IT DOES :
Optional, OFF by default (RESOLVE_STOCK=no). When on, install augments an
official package's deps with its stock deps, read from a precomputed sqlite db
(depgraph.db, built by minotavros, fetched from STOCK_DB_URL). The extra deps go
through the SAME plan/prompt path as everything else - shown as `new dep for
<parent>`. slacker still never guesses: it reads a real linked+runtime dep graph,
official packages still ship no auto-dep metadata.

WHY:
A full-ISO Slackware has every stock .so already, so it's a no-op there. But a
minimal/container image (small Docker etc.) is missing them, and stock packages
assume they're present and never declare them. resolve-stock closes that gap
without dragging in a foreign package manager or changing the tradition.

- New module src/stockdb.rs: the edges∪hints query (build-time hints EXCLUDED,
  deduped), db validation, README/ChangeLog freshness stamps. Uses rusqlite with
  the `bundled` feature so sqlite is compiled in - runtime stays glibc-only, no
  system libsqlite3. (5th direct dep, only for this.)
- install: add_with_deps appends the stock deps for official packages, gated
  inside the existing `if resolve` block (--no-deps / RESOLVE_DEPS=no disables it
  too). Missing db --> one warning, continues without stock deps - never a silent
  half-install, never a hard stop.
- update: fetches + validates the db from STOCK_DB_URL on EVERY update (missing or
  stale is always refreshed, even when all repos are up-to-date). Atomic
  temp+rename so a bad download never clobbers a good db. Reports in-sync /
  behind / failed by comparing the source README stamp to the official ChangeLog
  head - never stops the run.
- status: one `Stock-db` row in the Online section (present/valid/in-sync,
  behind, invalid, or "no database installed"). Hidden when the switch is off.

The stock-db is NOT a repo: no PACKAGES.TXT/CHECKSUMS, no priority, never in the
install path. It's a read-only, stock-only source under STATE_DIR
(/var/lib/slacker/stock/depgraph.db, persistent - not the disposable cache).

New conf keys: RESOLVE_STOCK (default no) + STOCK_DB_URL.
With RESOLVE_STOCK off, behaviour is unchanged in every command.

Add: 9 unit tests in stockdb.rs (in-file sqlite, no network/root) - 201 total.
Update: DEV docs (structure.md, CODE_MAP.txt).
Update: Add wiki docker page.
Update: cmd: `slacker status` now also check for mlocate if outdated and inform.
        Fix: AI suggest `re-run with sudo` but in slackware is better to suggest `re-run as root`
---

Version Beta 0.10.3
=====
- Updates: Thanks to @danix !!!
  - New: bash tab-completion for all 38 subcommands. Completes flags,
  installed package names, repo names, @repo / @_tag selectors,
  template names, and pin's `repo:` prefix. Installed by the package
  to /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/slacker and loaded
  automatically in new shells. First external contribution - thanks
  to danix! (PR #3)
  - Completion ignores leftover `-upgraded-<timestamp>` records in
  /var/adm/packages, so an interrupted upgradepkg never produces
  phantom names or garbage tags at the prompt.
  - Developer tooling: contrib/check-completion-drift.sh verifies the
  completion's command list against the live `slacker --help`; the
  SlackBuild now runs it after the tests, so a stale completion
  fails the build instead of shipping. (repo-only, not installed)
  - New: zsh and fish completions alongside bash - all three now
  generated from a single source of truth (contrib/completions.json,
  rendered by contrib/gen-completions.py; python3 at build time only,
  nothing at runtime). Fixes two arg-type bugs of the hand-written
  bash: install-new now completes bare repo names (not @repo), and
  upgrade-all no longer offers selectors (it takes no argument).
  Installed to /usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_slacker and
  /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/slacker.fish. (PR #4)
  - The SlackBuild now also runs gen-completions.py --check, so a
  generated completion that doesn't match its JSON source fails the
  build; together with the drift-check this means completions can
  never silently drift from the binary.
Note: bash requires the bash-completion package (Slackware extra/) for automatic loading - install it with slacker install bash-completion from an extras subtree repo, or source the file from your shell rc. zsh and fish need nothing extra. If you have in use the old style "complete -cf sudo" sudo dont follow correctly you must disable it.
